Package: aptwarden-helper
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: ramhee98 <32970397+ramhee98@users.noreply.github.com>
Depends: sudo, passwd, apt
Recommends: needrestart
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/ramhee98/aptwarden
Description: root helper for aptwarden on patched Debian hosts
 aptwarden scans Debian hosts over SSH for vulnerable packages and patches
 them. On a target host, every action that needs root goes through this
 small POSIX sh helper. sudo allows the user aptwarden to run it and nothing
 else. It has fixed subcommands, validates every package=version argument,
 and installs only exactly the simulated versions from the host's own apt
 sources.
 .
 The package installs the helper, writes /etc/sudoers.d/aptwarden and
 creates the user aptwarden if it is missing. The central host's SSH key
 still has to be added to ~aptwarden/.ssh/authorized_keys.
